.TH CHANGELOG-INIT 8 "July 2026" "changelog 1.0.0" "System Administration Commands"
.SH NAME
changelog init \- initialize changelog infrastructure for a project
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B changelog init
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIproject\-root\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBinit\fR command bootstraps a new changelog directory structure with
default configuration. It creates the standard layout expected by other
changelog commands and writes a sample config file that users can customize.

After initialization, projects should have:
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
\fIchangelogs/config.yaml\fR \- Configuration file with project settings
.IP \(bu 2
\fIchangelogs/fragments/\fR \- Directory for fragment files
.RE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show help message and exit.

.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Increase verbosity of output messages.

.TP
\fB\-\-is\-other\-project\fR
Mark this as a wrapper project rather than the primary upstream. When set,
the generated config will include settings appropriate for projects that
consume changelogs from dependencies (e.g., Ansible collections wrapping
upstream plugins).

Defaults to \fIfalse\fR unless explicitly specified.
.SH POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
.TP
\fIproject\-root\fR
Path to the project root directory where changelog infrastructure should be created.
.PP
If not provided, defaults to the current working directory (\fB.\fR). The command will
create a \fIchangelogs/\fR subdirectory structure within this path.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Initialize in current directory:
.nf
    changelog init
.fi

.TP
Initialize in a specific project directory:
.nf
    changelog init /path/to/myproject
.fi

.TP
Initialize as an "other" (wrapper) project:
.nf
    changelog init --is-other-project mycollection
.fi
.SH OUTPUT
.PP
On success, the command prints confirmation messages showing which files were created:
.IP \(bu 2
\fI[changelogs/config.yaml]\fR \- Configuration file with defaults
.IP \(bu 2
\fI[changelogs/fragments/\fR] \- Empty fragments directory ready for use
.PP
The generated config includes sensible defaults that can be customized by editing
\fIchangelogs/config.yaml\fR directly. See \fBchangelog\-config(5)\fR for configuration options.
.SH SEE ALSO
.TP
\fBchangelog-add(8)\fR \- Create new fragment files
.TP
\fBchangelog-release(8)\fR \- Generate release changelogs from fragments
.TP
\fBchangelog-config(5)\fR \- Configuration file reference
